FN-9JVVYBM-1
FISCAL NOTE
House Bill 460
Committee: Ways and Means General Fund Sponsor: Representative Rex Reynolds
Analyst: Tiffany Weaver Date: 03/31/2025
House Bill 460 as introduced would appropriate a total of $41,059,071 from the Opioid
Treatment and Abatement Fund for fiscal year 2025 to the following entities in the following
amounts:
 Department of Corrections: $900,000;
 Board of Pardons and Paroles: $120,000;
 Department of Mental Health: $27,860,000;
 Auburn University: $1 million;
 University of Alabama at Birmingham: $1 million;
 USA Health University of South Alabama: $1 million;
 Department of Public Health: $500,000;
 Administrative Office of Courts for Mental Health: $3 million;
 Department of Veterans Affairs: $1.5 million;
 Department of Human Resources: $500,000
 Office of Prosecution Services: $2.6 million;
 Department of Forensic Sciences: $800,000;
 Department of Senior Services: $279,071.
This bill would also provide that these funds would not revert at the end of fiscal year 2025 but
would carry forward for the purposes appropriated.
